  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Banco Internacional Blue Bond</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IFC anticipates that the Project will increase access to climate finance, in particular blue economy projects aligned to international standards. 

Being part of a programmatic set of interventions from both the IFC and the WB that aim to increase Blue Finance in the country, beyond the project-level impact, IFC anticipates that the investment will contribute to greater market sustainability by promoting a new asset class following and disseminating the recently published IFC Blue Finance Guideline Framework in line with ICMAs Green Bond Principles.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed project entails a blue bond to be issued by Banco Internacional (Internacional or the Bank) in the Ecuadorian local bond market, which will be subscribed by IFC. The blue bond proceeds will be used by the Bank to promote a sustainable blue economy and management of clean-water resources.</narrative>
  </description>
